# Security + cache headers for docs.aevumfinance.com (Cloudflare Pages, Netlify-compatible).
#
# Mirrors aevum-web's posture (T-docs-site D7): the four security headers below are
# STATIC and hand-authored; the Content-Security-Policy is NOT here — it is generated
# at build time by scripts/emit-csp.mjs and APPENDED to dist/_headers, because its
# script-src carries the sha256 of the inline no-FOUC bootstrap (Base.astro), derived
# from the built HTML so a hand-pasted hash can never drift. Look at dist/_headers
# after a build to see the CSP that actually ships. Fail-open: if the emitter doesn't
# run, the site ships with the static headers and NO CSP rather than a broken one.
#
# HSTS is set once at the Cloudflare edge (SSL/TLS → HSTS, includeSubDomains covers
# this subdomain), exactly as aevum-web does — not here, which would only reach Pages.

/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()

# The /data feeds are a public contract (D6): open CORS so a downstream can fetch
# them client-side, with a short cache so a fold shows up within the hour.
/data/*
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

/images/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/brand/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/manual/user_manual.pdf
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

# Astro's hashed asset bundles are immutable.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
